E1: --defwriter, the definition-item writer (prereg v4 block H-a)

HoldMem(def_writer=..., def_max_tokens=...): as in the D0think arm, the
pre-shift snapshot and every other item use the main writer (same
requests); definition items written after the shift (B=1 re-derivations,
B=0 delta derivations, refreshes) in every cell come from the second
client with the same request text and its own output limit. A reply cut
off by the limit (finish reason length or max_tokens) is unreadable
(derive(reasoning=True)). Each such item records model, ok, completion
tokens and at_limit in its note; every cell counts these writes in
def_stats (B=0 drops unreadable delta writes), reported per branch in
world_summaries. Keys keep the main writer's id.

The E1 driver builds client(MODEL, run_dir, extra_body=...) with, for
claude-* models, extra_body {thinking: enabled, budget_tokens 16000} and
max_tokens 17000 (defwriter_settings), records defwriter in the manifest
(models and params) and refuses --defwriter with D0think cells.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
